Scott's smash combinator equals the canonical subsystem retraction of the smash subsystem of the product.

Compare membership by the closed form of smash and the closed form of the subsystem retraction. If the neighbourhood is the master, the smash master is a witness. If both coordinates are not bottom and the neighbourhood belongs to z, the compactness lemma supplies a smash witness. Conversely, a witness that is the smash master forces the neighbourhood to be the product master, and a proper product witness has factors belonging to the two coordinates, so neither coordinate is bottom, and upward closure puts the neighbourhood in z.
